  "final_message": "I haven't made this change, because the field is still read in several places. Removing it would break at least one other team's service.\n\n**Other teams (read-only checkouts)**\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` requires `channel` on `OrderPlaced` and rejects the whole event if it's missing or unknown. Its README (line 27–31) lists it as part of the contract. `ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `orders.channel` column. If we dropped it, every `OrderPlaced` event would be rejected.\n- `billing-service` only sets `channel` in its test helpers. I didn't see it used in its source, but I only searched for the string.\n\n**This repo**\n- `src/api/legacyExport.ts:6,18` still exports `channel` as a CSV column. `test/adapters.test.ts:137` asserts on that header.\n- `src/core/order.ts` and `src/api/requestParsing.ts` validate `channel` and require it on `POST /orders`. That's part of the API documented in `CLAUDE.md` and the README.\n\nHow would you like to proceed? The options I can see:\n1. Do a coordinated rollout. analytics-ingest first makes `channel` optional or drops it, and then we remove it here. I can only edit orders-service.\n2. Remove it from the order model and the API input only, and keep emitting it on the event with a fixed default. That seems pointless, so I'd rather not.\n3. Go ahead and remove it everywhere in orders-service anyway, if you've confirmed analytics-ingest is being updated separately. That includes the legacy export column and the tests.",
